    %%report compound-completeness title: How complete compounds are entity: Compound chart: bar x: field y: missing help: One registered chemical structure. For each optional field, how many compounds leave it empty; the long bars are the fields nobody fills in. sql: SELECT 'inchi key' AS field, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE inchi_key IS NULL) AS missing FROM bus_compound WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'common name', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE common_name IS NULL) FROM bus_compound WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'cas number', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE cas_number IS NULL) FROM bus_compound WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'formula', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE formula IS NULL) FROM bus_compound WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'compound series', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE compound_series_id IS NULL) FROM bus_compound WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'molecular weight', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE molecular_weight IS NULL) FROM bus_compound WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'logp', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE logp IS NULL) FROM bus_compound WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'tpsa', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE tpsa IS NULL) FROM bus_compound WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY 2 DESC
    %%report assay-by-assay-type title: Assays by assay type entity: Assay chart: pie x: assay_type y: records help: A defined way of measuring something about a compound. How assays divide across assay type, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(assay_type::text, '(unset)') AS assay_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_assay WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
