    %%report admet-profile-caco2-permeability-per-month title: Average caco2 permeability per month entity: AdmetProfile chart: line x: month y: average_caco2_permeability help: What is known about whether a compound could behave like a drug — absorption, distribution, metabolism, excretion and toxicity. The average caco2 permeability of admet profiles created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(caco2_permeability)::numeric, 2) AS average_caco2_permeability FROM bus_admet_profile WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
    %%report admet-profile-largest-by-caco2-permeability title: The ten largest admet profiles by caco2 permeability entity: AdmetProfile chart: bar x: record y: caco2_permeability help: What is known about whether a compound could behave like a drug — absorption, distribution, metabolism, excretion and toxicity. The records with the highest caco2 permeability; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT ames_result::text AS record, caco2_permeability FROM bus_admet_profile WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND caco2_permeability IS NOT NULL ORDER BY caco2_permeability DESC LIMIT 10
    %%report admet-profile-microsomal-half-life-min-by-ames-result title: Total microsomal half life min by ames result entity: AdmetProfile chart: bar x: ames_result y: total_microsomal_half_life_min help: What is known about whether a compound could behave like a drug — absorption, distribution, metabolism, excretion and toxicity. Admet Profiles added up on microsomal half life min, split by ames result, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(ames_result::text, '(unset)') AS ames_result, ROUND(SUM(microsomal_half_life_min)::numeric, 2) AS total_microsomal_half_life_min FROM bus_admet_profile WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
    %%report admet-profile-microsomal-half-life-min-per-month title: Average microsomal half life min per month entity: AdmetProfile chart: line x: month y: average_microsomal_half_life_min help: What is known about whether a compound could behave like a drug — absorption, distribution, metabolism, excretion and toxicity. The average microsomal half life min of admet profiles created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(microsomal_half_life_min)::numeric, 2) AS average_microsomal_half_life_min FROM bus_admet_profile WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
    %%report admet-profile-largest-by-microsomal-half-life-min title: The ten largest admet profiles by microsomal half life min entity: AdmetProfile chart: bar x: record y: microsomal_half_life_min help: What is known about whether a compound could behave like a drug — absorption, distribution, metabolism, excretion and toxicity. The records with the highest microsomal half life min; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT ames_result::text AS record, microsomal_half_life_min FROM bus_admet_profile WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND microsomal_half_life_min IS NOT NULL ORDER BY microsomal_half_life_min DESC LIMIT 10
    %%report experiment-by-status title: Experiments by status entity: Experiment chart: bar x: status y: records help: A planned piece of laboratory work, reviewed and approved before it runs. How experiments divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_experiment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
    %%report experiment-lifecycle title: Experiment lifecycle entity: Experiment chart: bar x: state y: records help: A planned piece of laboratory work, reviewed and approved before it runs. Where experiments sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'draft' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'submitted', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'in_review', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'approved', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'in_progress', 4 UNION ALL SELECT 'completed', 5 UNION ALL SELECT 'on_hold', 6 UNION ALL SELECT 'cancelled', 7) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_experiment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
    %%report experiment-created-per-month title: Experiments created per month entity: Experiment chart: line x: month y: records help: A planned piece of laboratory work, reviewed and approved before it runs. New experiments per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_experiment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
    %%report experiment-created-by-weekday title: Experiments created by day of the week entity: Experiment chart: bar x: weekday y: records help: A planned piece of laboratory work, reviewed and approved before it runs. Which days experiments are recorded on, which is the working rhythm of the people who enter them. sql: SELECT to_char(created_at, 'Dy') AS weekday, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_experiment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1, EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at) ORDER BY EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at)
    %%report experiment-changed-per-month title: Experiments last changed per month entity: Experiment chart: line x: month y: records help: A planned piece of laboratory work, reviewed and approved before it runs. How recently experiments were touched - a falling line is a register nobody is keeping up. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', updated_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_experiment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND updated_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
    %%report experiment-age-bands title: How recently experiments were changed entity: Experiment chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: A planned piece of laboratory work, reviewed and approved before it runs. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_experiment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
    %%report experiment-edit-churn title: How often experiments are edited entity: Experiment chart: bar x: edits y: records help: A planned piece of laboratory work, reviewed and approved before it runs. Records by how many times they have been saved; the heavily edited ones are where the process is being fought. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN version <= 1 THEN 'never edited' WHEN version <= 3 THEN 'edited once or twice' WHEN version <= 9 THEN 'edited 3 to 8 times' ELSE 'edited 9 or more times' END AS edits, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_experiment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(version)
    %%report experiment-removed-per-month title: Experiments removed per month entity: Experiment chart: line x: month y: removed help: A planned piece of laboratory work, reviewed and approved before it runs. Records withdrawn from use each month; a rising line means the register is being cleared faster than it is kept. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', deleted_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS removed FROM bus_experiment WHERE deleted_at IS NOT NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
    %%report experiment-submitted-at-per-month title: Experiments by submitted at entity: Experiment chart: line x: month y: records help: A planned piece of laboratory work, reviewed and approved before it runs. Experiments grouped by the month of submitted at, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', submitted_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_experiment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND submitted_at IS NOT NULL AND submitted_at >= now() - interval '24 months' AND submitted_at < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
    %%report experiment-completed-at-per-month title: Experiments by completed at entity: Experiment chart: line x: month y: records help: A planned piece of laboratory work, reviewed and approved before it runs. Experiments grouped by the month of completed at, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', completed_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_experiment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND completed_at IS NOT NULL AND completed_at >= now() - interval '24 months' AND completed_at < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
    %%report experiment-in-review-at-per-month title: Experiments by in review at entity: Experiment chart: line x: month y: records help: A planned piece of laboratory work, reviewed and approved before it runs. Experiments grouped by the month of in review at, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', in_review_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_experiment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND in_review_at IS NOT NULL AND in_review_at >= now() - interval '24 months' AND in_review_at < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
    %%report experiment-is-gmp-critical-share title: Experiments: is gmp critical entity: Experiment chart: pie x: is_gmp_critical y: records help: A planned piece of laboratory work, reviewed and approved before it runs. The share of experiments where is gmp critical holds against those where it does not. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN is_gmp_critical THEN 'yes' ELSE 'no' END AS is_gmp_critical, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_experiment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
    %%report experiment-estimated-duration-days-by-status title: Total estimated duration days by status entity: Experiment chart: bar x: status y: total_estimated_duration_days help: A planned piece of laboratory work, reviewed and approved before it runs. Experiments added up on estimated duration days, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(estimated_duration_days)::numeric, 2) AS total_estimated_duration_days FROM bus_experiment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
    %%report experiment-estimated-duration-days-per-month title: Average estimated duration days per month entity: Experiment chart: line x: month y: average_estimated_duration_days help: A planned piece of laboratory work, reviewed and approved before it runs. The average estimated duration days of experiments created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(estimated_duration_days)::numeric, 2) AS average_estimated_duration_days FROM bus_experiment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
    %%report experiment-largest-by-estimated-duration-days title: The ten largest experiments by estimated duration days entity: Experiment chart: bar x: record y: estimated_duration_days help: A planned piece of laboratory work, reviewed and approved before it runs. The records with the highest estimated duration days; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT title::text AS record, estimated_duration_days FROM bus_experiment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND estimated_duration_days IS NOT NULL ORDER BY estimated_duration_days DESC LIMIT 10
    %%report experiment-completeness title: How complete experiments are entity: Experiment chart: bar x: field y: missing help: A planned piece of laboratory work, reviewed and approved before it runs. For each optional field, how many experiments leave it empty; the long bars are the fields nobody fills in. sql: SELECT 'program' AS field, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE program_id IS NULL) AS missing FROM bus_experiment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'project code', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE project_code IS NULL) FROM bus_experiment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'estimated duration days', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE estimated_duration_days IS NULL) FROM bus_experiment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'submitted at', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE submitted_at IS NULL) FROM bus_experiment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'completed at', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE completed_at IS NULL) FROM bus_experiment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'objective', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE objective IS NULL) FROM bus_experiment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'in review at', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE in_review_at IS NULL) FROM bus_experiment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'draft at', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE draft_at IS NULL) FROM bus_experiment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY 2 DESC
    %%report sample-by-status title: Samples by status entity: Sample chart: pie x: status y: records help: A physical quantity of material in a tube, plate or vial, in a known place. How samples divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_sample WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
    %%report sample-by-physical-state title: Samples by physical state entity: Sample chart: pie x: physical_state y: records help: A physical quantity of material in a tube, plate or vial, in a known place. How samples divide across physical state, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(physical_state::text, '(unset)') AS physical_state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_sample WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
    %%report sample-top-storage-location title: Samples: the most common storage location entity: Sample chart: bar x: storage_location y: records help: A physical quantity of material in a tube, plate or vial, in a known place. The ten most frequent values of storage location among samples; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(storage_location, '(blank)') AS storage_location, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_sample WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
    %%report inventory-transaction-by-transaction-type title: Inventory Transactions by transaction type entity: InventoryTransaction chart: pie x: transaction_type y: records help: One movement of material — received, split into aliquots, consumed, moved, discarded or corrected. How inventory transactions divide across transaction type, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(transaction_type::text, '(unset)') AS transaction_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_inventory_transaction WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
    %%report inventory-transaction-top-from-location title: Inventory Transactions: the most common from location entity: InventoryTransaction chart: bar x: from_location y: records help: One movement of material — received, split into aliquots, consumed, moved, discarded or corrected. The ten most frequent values of from location among inventory transactions; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(from_location, '(blank)') AS from_location, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_inventory_transaction WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
    %%report inventory-transaction-top-to-location title: Inventory Transactions: the most common to location entity: InventoryTransaction chart: bar x: to_location y: records help: One movement of material — received, split into aliquots, consumed, moved, discarded or corrected. The ten most frequent values of to location among inventory transactions; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(to_location, '(blank)') AS to_location, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_inventory_transaction WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
    %%report instrument-by-instrument-type title: Instruments by instrument type entity: Instrument chart: bar x: instrument_type y: records help: A piece of laboratory equipment that produces data. How instruments divide across instrument type, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(instrument_type::text, '(unset)') AS instrument_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_instrument WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
    %%report instrument-by-calibration-status title: Instruments by calibration status entity: Instrument chart: pie x: calibration_status y: records help: A piece of laboratory equipment that produces data. How instruments divide across calibration status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(calibration_status::text, '(unset)') AS calibration_status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_instrument WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
