    %%report instrument-is-active-share title: Instruments: is active entity: Instrument chart: pie x: is_active y: records help: A piece of laboratory equipment that produces data. The share of instruments where is active holds against those where it does not. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN is_active THEN 'yes' ELSE 'no' END AS is_active, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_instrument WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
    %%report instrument-top-location title: Instruments: the most common location entity: Instrument chart: bar x: location y: records help: A piece of laboratory equipment that produces data. The ten most frequent values of location among instruments; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(location, '(blank)') AS location, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_instrument WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
    %%report instrument-booking-by-status title: Instrument Bookings by status entity: InstrumentBooking chart: pie x: status y: records help: A reserved block of time on an instrument. How instrument bookings divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_instrument_booking WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
    %%report instrument-booking-per-instrument title: Instrument Bookings per instrument entity: InstrumentBooking chart: bar x: instrument y: records help: A reserved block of time on an instrument. Which instrument the most instrument bookings belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS instrument, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_instrument_booking x LEFT JOIN bus_instrument p ON p.id = x.instrument_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
    %%report instrument-booking-per-experiment title: Instrument Bookings per experiment entity: InstrumentBooking chart: bar x: experiment y: records help: A reserved block of time on an instrument. Which experiment the most instrument bookings belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.title::text, '(none)') AS experiment, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_instrument_booking x LEFT JOIN bus_experiment p ON p.id = x.experiment_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
    %%report vendor-by-sla-tier title: Vendors by sla tier entity: Vendor chart: pie x: sla_tier y: records help: An external supplier or contract research organisation. How vendors divide across sla tier, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(sla_tier::text, '(unset)') AS sla_tier, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_vendor WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
