    %%report vendor-request-by-status title: Vendor Requests by status entity: VendorRequest chart: bar x: status y: records help: A piece of work sent outside — a synthesis, a panel, an analysis. How vendor requests divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_vendor_request WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
    %%report vendor-request-quoted-cost-by-status title: Total quoted cost by status entity: VendorRequest chart: bar x: status y: total_quoted_cost help: A piece of work sent outside — a synthesis, a panel, an analysis. Vendor Requests added up on quoted cost, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(quoted_cost)::numeric, 2) AS total_quoted_cost FROM bus_vendor_request WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
    %%report vendor-request-quoted-cost-per-month title: Average quoted cost per month entity: VendorRequest chart: line x: month y: average_quoted_cost help: A piece of work sent outside — a synthesis, a panel, an analysis. The average quoted cost of vendor requests created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(quoted_cost)::numeric, 2) AS average_quoted_cost FROM bus_vendor_request WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
    %%report deviation-report-by-status title: Deviation Reports by status entity: DeviationReport chart: pie x: status y: records help: A record that something did not go to plan. How deviation reports divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_deviation_report WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
    %%report deviation-report-by-severity title: Deviation Reports by severity entity: DeviationReport chart: pie x: severity y: records help: A record that something did not go to plan. How deviation reports divide across severity, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(severity::text, '(unset)') AS severity, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_deviation_report WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
