    %%report capa-in-progress-at-per-month title: CAPAs by in progress at entity: CAPA chart: line x: month y: records help: A corrective and preventive action — what was done about a deviation, and what stops it happening again. CAPAs grouped by the month of in progress at, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', in_progress_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_capa WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND in_progress_at IS NOT NULL AND in_progress_at >= now() - interval '24 months' AND in_progress_at < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
    %%report capa-pending-verification-at-per-month title: CAPAs by pending verification at entity: CAPA chart: line x: month y: records help: A corrective and preventive action — what was done about a deviation, and what stops it happening again. CAPAs grouped by the month of pending verification at, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', pending_verification_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_capa WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND pending_verification_at IS NOT NULL AND pending_verification_at >= now() - interval '24 months' AND pending_verification_at < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
    %%report capa-effectiveness-metric-by-status title: Total effectiveness metric by status entity: CAPA chart: bar x: status y: total_effectiveness_metric help: A corrective and preventive action — what was done about a deviation, and what stops it happening again. CAPAs added up on effectiveness metric, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(effectiveness_metric)::numeric, 2) AS total_effectiveness_metric FROM bus_capa WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
    %%report capa-effectiveness-metric-per-month title: Average effectiveness metric per month entity: CAPA chart: line x: month y: average_effectiveness_metric help: A corrective and preventive action — what was done about a deviation, and what stops it happening again. The average effectiveness metric of capas created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(effectiveness_metric)::numeric, 2) AS average_effectiveness_metric FROM bus_capa WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
    %%report capa-largest-by-effectiveness-metric title: The ten largest capas by effectiveness metric entity: CAPA chart: bar x: record y: effectiveness_metric help: A corrective and preventive action — what was done about a deviation, and what stops it happening again. The records with the highest effectiveness metric; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT title::text AS record, effectiveness_metric FROM bus_capa WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND effectiveness_metric IS NOT NULL ORDER BY effectiveness_metric DESC LIMIT 10
    %%report capa-per-deviation-report title: CAPAs per deviation report entity: CAPA chart: bar x: deviation_report y: records help: A corrective and preventive action — what was done about a deviation, and what stops it happening again. Which deviation report the most capas belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.severity::text, '(none)') AS deviation_report, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_capa x LEFT JOIN bus_deviation_report p ON p.id = x.deviation_report_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
    %%report capa-effectiveness-metric-per-deviation-report title: Total effectiveness metric per deviation report entity: CAPA chart: bar x: deviation_report y: total_effectiveness_metric help: A corrective and preventive action — what was done about a deviation, and what stops it happening again. CAPAs added up on effectiveness metric for each deviation report, ten largest first. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.severity::text, '(none)') AS deviation_report, ROUND(SUM(x.effectiveness_metric)::numeric, 2) AS total_effectiveness_metric FROM bus_capa x LEFT JOIN bus_deviation_report p ON p.id = x.deviation_report_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST LIMIT 10
    %%report user-by-role title: Users by role entity: User chart: bar x: role y: records help: Somebody who works in the laboratory or on the portfolio. How users divide across role, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(role::text, '(unset)') AS role, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_user WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
    %%report user-per-team title: Users per team entity: User chart: bar x: team y: records help: Somebody who works in the laboratory or on the portfolio. Which team the most users belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS team, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_user x LEFT JOIN bus_team p ON p.id = x.team_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
    %%report user-top-department title: Users: the most common department entity: User chart: bar x: department y: records help: Somebody who works in the laboratory or on the portfolio. The ten most frequent values of department among users; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(department, '(blank)') AS department, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_user WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
    %%report team-created-per-month title: Teams created per month entity: Team chart: line x: month y: records help: A group of people who work together, usually around a technique or a programme. New teams per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_team WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
    %%report team-top-department title: Teams: the most common department entity: Team chart: bar x: department y: records help: A group of people who work together, usually around a technique or a programme. The ten most frequent values of department among teams; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(department, '(blank)') AS department, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_team WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
    %%report team-completeness title: How complete teams are entity: Team chart: bar x: field y: missing help: A group of people who work together, usually around a technique or a programme. For each optional field, how many teams leave it empty; the long bars are the fields nobody fills in. sql: SELECT 'manager' AS field, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE manager_id IS NULL) AS missing FROM bus_team WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'department', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE department IS NULL) FROM bus_team WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY 2 DESC
